WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.500
 

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:08.700
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.120
 

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:13.810
DAVE WILLIAMS: A matrix diagram is
a tool used to arrange and display

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:17.320
information in order to help you
understand important relationships

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:18.700
and make decisions.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.880
It can be used in a
number of different ways

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.020
to help you make decisions for action.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:27.400
For example, imagine you're
looking at a list of change ideas.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.050
You know you have only so much capacity.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.240
And you want to be thoughtful
about where to start.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.870
You might use a matrix
diagram like this.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:35.956
Let's draw this out.

00:00:35.956 --> 00:00:44.090
 

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:48.320
So what I can do here is basically
say, OK, I've got my different ideas.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.640
And with my team, I can
look and say, well, gosh,

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.940
let me think about
this here for a second.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:59.160
So with Idea 1, on a scale
of one to five, how much

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.205
do we think this can be done
in, say, a 90 day time frame?

00:01:02.205 --> 00:01:04.330
We might look at that and
say, oh, gosh, I can only

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.620
do-- this may take longer than 90 days.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:09.272
I'm not sure, so maybe
I'll give that one a two.

00:01:09.272 --> 00:01:14.670
On Idea 2, though, I think this one
totally could get done in 90 days.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.460
And Idea 3, there's
probably a high likelihood.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:17.960
OK.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:18.459
Great.

00:01:18.459 --> 00:01:20.844
Well, let me think about
will to fix this problem?

00:01:20.844 --> 00:01:22.010
Is this important to people?

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:24.690
I might come here and say, well,
you know there's a lot of will

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:27.360
here for an Idea 1.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:30.240
There's actually quite a bit for Idea 2.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.890
But Idea 3, you know,
it's something that people

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:34.270
aren't ready to work on yet.

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:38.680
And then as I look at things that
I have control to make changes on,

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:40.710
I might come across and say, OK, great.

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:43.870
This again, maybe it's moderate
level to control the changes.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.870
This one, pretty much
completely in my control.

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:50.200
And Idea 3 is not in my control at all.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.250
And then sponsorship, I
look and Idea 1, there's

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:58.360
a sponsor who says that this would
make sense and they'll look at it.

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:00.790
There's good sponsorship for Idea 2.

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:05.640
And there's limited sponsorship,
moderate sponsorship for Idea 3.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:09.460
So as I'm looking at my matrix,
now I can kind of look at my data

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:12.920
and say, well, which of these ideas
has the best chance of success, right?

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.700
And in this particular
case, as I look across them,

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:20.470
I might decide to select Idea 2, because
I've got a higher degree of belief

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:23.470
that it's going to be able to be
accomplished in a short amount of time,

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:27.750
there's will to improve it, I have the
ability or the control to test changes,

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:29.010
and there's good sponsorship.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:34.700
So that's a high spot for me to
potentially be successful in a project.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.900
As you go through the
ranking, you hopefully

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.820
discover that one change
idea may be better

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:42.060
than another to start
with because it possesses

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:44.460
more of the factors for success.

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:47.000
It also can help you
think about where work

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:51.020
may need to occur to improve the
likelihood of success of other change

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.250
ideas before you begin to test them.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:58.700
Can you think of where in your project
a matrix diagram could be useful?

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:12.887
 

